is stronger still: `closeStep` is idempotent on **every** pair,\n594\t  empty or not (`closeStep_closeStep`), because `A ⊆ V ∖ N[V ∖ N[A]]` holds\n595\t  for every `A` (`subset_compl_closedNbhd_compl_closedNbhd`). Emptiness is\n596\t  needed only for monotonicity in `R` (`subset_closeStep`).\n597\t* **The pair form suffices for Theorem S**, as §8.4 said; `IsBalancedBip` is\n598\t  the pair form, and the component form appears only in L1′ (b).\n599\t* **`|R| = n − k − t` is written `(n − k) / 2`**, equal in `ℕ` arithmetic\n600\t  (`omega`); the item's expression is the same number.\n601\t* **(d) fitted**, against the item's expectation, and so did the\n602\t  relabelling the item did not ask for; the named `Prop`\n603\t  `SeparatorFactorisation` was not needed.\n604\t* **`decide` cannot do `IsBalancedBip` directly**: over `64 × 64` pairs of\n605\t  subsets it hits the recursion limit; reducing to the 64 subsets `A`\n606\t  (`R = univ \\ A` is forced) and `decide +kernel` settles it in under a\n607\t  second. `native_decide` was not used (it would add an axiom).\n608\t* **`componentOff` is not Mathlib's `ConnectedComponent`**: it is the\n609\t  reachable set through walks avoiding `S`, as a `Finset` under classical\n610\t  decidability. The two agree (a walk in `G.induce (V ∖ S)` is a walk of `G`\n611\t  avoiding `S`), but the equivalence is not proved here and nothing rests\n612\t  on it.\n613\t\n614\t### 10.6 Appendix A rows, drafted for item 12 (not in the paper)\n615\t\n616\t```latex\n617\t\\leanentry{separator}{Appendix~\\ref{app:random}, counting events: a layout of width $k<n$ forces pairwise disjoint $A,R,S$ covering $V$ with $|A|=\\lceil(n-k)/2\\rceil$, $|R|=\\lfloor(n-k)/2\\rfloor$, $|S|=k$ and no $A$--$R$ edge (on the MOSP graph: no pattern meets both $A$ and $R$); a walk avoiding $S$ that starts in $A$ stays in $A$, so every component of $G-S$ has at most $\\lceil(n-k)/2\\rceil$ vertices; $3K_2$ at $k=0$ satisfies the component condition and not the bipartition one} \\leannames{exists_balanced_separator, exists_balanced_separator_cover, exists_isBalancedBip, card_componentOff_le_of_isBalancedBip, not_isBalancedBip_threeK2, card_componentOff_threeK2_le} \\\\\n618\t\\leanentry{closedpair}{The closed pair: $R\\subseteq V\\setminus N[A]$ iff $(A,R)$ is disjoint and empty (the Galois step); one round of the alternating closure $R^{*}=V\\setminus N[A]$, $A^{*}=V\\setminus N[R^{*}]$ is monotone on empty pairs, lands on a closed pair ($A^{*}=V\\setminus N[R^{*}]$, $R^{*}=V\\setminus N[A^{*}]$) from every $A$, is idempotent, has separator $N(A^{*})\\cap N(R^{*})$ and keeps the sizes; a pair is closed iff it is empty and every outside vertex sees both sides; a layout of width $k<n$ forces a closed empty pair with sides of at least the forced sizes} \\leannames{subset_compl_closedNbhd_iff, subset_closeStep, closeStep_isClosedPair, closeStep_closeStep, sdiff_eq_inter_boundary_of_isClosedPair, card_closeStep, isClosedPair_iff_sees_both, exists_closedPair_of_pathwidth_le} \\\\\n619\t\\leanentry{weightedcount}{Lemma~W: for any weight $1\\le Z(P)\\le\\#\\{\\text{empty pairs}\\}$ on the empty pairs, $\\sum_P \\mathbf 1[P\\ \\text{empty}]/Z(P)\\ge\\mathbf 1[\\text{some pair is empty}]$, so $\\Pr[\\pw\\le k]\\le E[\\sum_P \\mathbf 1[P\\ \\text{empty}]/Z(G,P)]$ over the exact-size pairs; with $Z$ the number of flips of $P$ (exchanging equally many vertices isolated in $G[A]$ and $G[R]$ gives distinct empty pairs of the same sizes), the weighted count of Corollary~W-flip} \\leannames{weightedCount_ge_indicator, weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_weighted, flipPair_isEmptyPair, flipPair_injOn, card_flipPair, card_flips_le, weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_flipWeighted} \\\\\n620\t\\leanentry{theoremS}{Theorem~S, the separator first moment in finite form: for $0\\le p\\le1$ and $k<n$, $\\Pr[\\pw(G(n,p))\\le k]\\le\\binom nk\\,P_N(E_{\\mathrm{bip}})$, where $P_N(E_{\\mathrm{bip}})$ is the $G(N,p)$-weighted count, $N=n-k$, of the graphs on $V\\setminus S$ whose vertices split into an empty pair of sizes $\\lceil N/2\\rceil$, $\\lfloor N/2\\rfloor$; the union bound over the $\\binom nk$ separators is the only inequality: the graphs on $V$ with a given restriction to $V\\setminus S$ have total weight equal to the restriction's $G(N,p)$ weight (the pairs meeting $S$ carry weight $(p+(1-p))^{|\\text{pairs meeting }S|}=1$), and the inner count is the same for every $S$ by a relabelling of $V$} \\leannames{weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_choose_mul_innerBip, weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_separator, weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_sum_separators, sum_gnpWeight_fiber, sum_gnpWeight_bipGraphs, card_pairsOff, innerBip_eq_of_card_eq} \\\\\n621\t\\leanentry{theoremCl}{Theorem~Cl, the union bound: $\\Pr[\\pw\\le k]\\le\\sum_{(A,R)}\\Pr[(A,R)\\ \\text{is closed}]$ over the ordered disjoint pairs with $|A|\\ge\\lceil(n-k)/2\\rceil$, $|R|\\ge\\lfloor(n-k)/2\\rfloor$; the evaluation of each term as $(1-p)^{|A||R|}\\bigl((1-(1-p)^{|A|})(1-(1-p)^{|R|})\\bigr)^{|S|}$ is on paper} \\leannames{weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_sum_closedPairs} \\\\\n622\t```\n623\t\n624\tItem 12 should also add `SeparatorMoment.lean` to the file list in the\n625\tcomment at the head of `sec9e_appendix_random.tex`, and say in Appendix E\n626\tthat Theorem S is a Lean theorem and Theorem Cl's independence step is not.\n627\t\n628\t### 10.7 Regenerate, size range, kill verdict, what this does not claim\n629\t\n630\t* **Regenerate.** `cd lean && lake build` (the file builds in about 1.5 s\n631\t  on a built library); `make -C paper1/latex axioms`;\n632\t  `python -m learning.sandwich --stage separator` (1 s; add\n633\t  `--out <path>` to keep `reports/sandwich_tables.md` as the full run\n634\t  writes it) and `--stage lean` (the axiom audit through the sandwich\n635\t  path); `python3 -m pytest tests/test_separator_moment.py -k \"proved_names or close_step or sees_both or separator_check or three_k2\"`.\n636\t  Logs: `reports/scratch/separator_moment/10_lean/` (`lake_build.log`,\n637\t  `axiom_check.log`, `sandwich_separator.{md,log}`, `gate.log`).\n638\t* **Size range.** The theorems are for every finite `V`, every `k < n`,\n639\t  every `0 ≤ p ≤ 1` (Lean, no size). The numerical pin: 500 random graphs at\n640\t  `n = 5–11`; the transcription tests: every labelled graph to 5 vertices.\n641\t* **Kill verdict: none** (the item had none). Nothing left as a `Prop`;\n642\t  three groups of statements left on paper with their obstacles named in\n643\t  §10.3.\n644\t* **Does not claim.** Any value or rate of `P_N(E_bip)`: `innerBip` is a\n645\t  finite weighted sum, evaluated on paper by Lemma P (§5) and never in Lean.\n646\t  That Theorem Cl is in Lean: its union bound and characterisation step are,\n647\t  its independence step is not. That Corollary W-flip's right-hand side is\n648\t  evaluated: only `P ≤ E[Y]` with the flip weight is proved. That\n649\t  `componentOff` equals Mathlib's connected component (not proved, not\n650\t  used). That Lemma Fl's count is `C(|I_A| + |I_R|, |I_A|)`: only `1 ≤ #flips ≤ X`\n651\t  is proved, which is all admissibility needs. Nothing probabilistic beyond\n652\t  finite weighted counts; Propositions T and T-cover stay on paper with\n653\t  their hypotheses. Nothing re-solved; `solutions/` untouched.\n654\t\n655\t---\n656\t\n657\t## 11. The slack ledger: in stacks, what each count buys and what is left (item 11, 2026-11-01)\n658\t\n659\t*Item 11 of `Ralph_Loops/loop0011/iterations.md`. Deliverable:\n660\t`reports/scratch/separator_moment/11_ledger/` (`run.py` with stages\n661\t`covers`, `gnp`, `stats`, `draw`; `ledger_6_1.csv` and `ledger_gnp.csv`\n662\twith every instance's ladder; `cells_gnp.csv` with every `(n, k)` bound on\n663\tthe pilot cells; `summary.csv`; `ladder.png`; `run.log`);\n664\t`learning/separator_moment.py` extended (`harper_bound_graph`, the graph\n665\tform of Harper's bound on the `vs` scale; `floor_pw`; `layout_vertex_separation`);\n666\t`tests/test_separator_moment.py` (4 new tests, 91 in the module).\n667\tRegenerate: `nice -n 19 python3 reports/scratch/separator_moment/11_ledger/run.py --workers 6`.*\n668\t\n669\t**The question.** For a reader of the paper: on certified instances, how\n670\tfar is each count's floor from the pathwidth, and where does the remaining\n671\tslack sit — in the union bound (floor to Harper) or in the necessary\n672\tcondition (Harper to pathwidth)? §8.5 (b) of `excess_phase_diagram.md`\n673\tanswered it for the single pair on the `(6, 1)` covers; this section puts\n674\tevery count of this loop on the same ladder and adds the `G(n, c/n)` side.\n675\t\n676\t### 11.1 The ladder, and the conventions\n677\t\n678\tEverything here is on the **pathwidth scale**: `pw = optimum − 1` on\n679\tcovers (Yanasse's equality, `MOSPGraph.lean`), the proved width on the\n680\tpilot graphs. A **floor at threshold `θ`** is the largest `k` with the\n681\tcount's bound on `P(pw ≤ k)` below `θ`, plus one — \"`pw ≥ k + 1` unless\n682\tan event of probability below `θ` occurred\" (`floor_pw`; the record's\n683\t`learning.first_moment.floors` is this plus one more, for the optimum).\n684\t`< 0.01` is the floor the paper quotes; `< 1` is a statement with up to\n685\t99% failure probability and is carried for the record only. Per instance\n686\tthe ladder is\n687\t\n688\t    old pair → exact-size pair → best count → Harper → pw,\n689\t\n690\twith the *best count* `max(closed, flip, exact-size)` on covers and\n691\t`max(separator, closed, exact-size)` on `G(n, c/n)`. Each rung is the\n692\tfloor of the named count on *that instance's own sizes* (covers: the\n693\tempirical pattern sizes and `m`; graphs: the cell's `n` and `p`, so the\n694\tfour count rungs are the same for every graph of a cell and only Harper\n695\tand `pw` vary).\n696\t\n697\t**Harper** is the vertex-isoperimetric bound `vs ≥ max_i (i − M(i))`,\n698\t`M(i) = max{t : f(t) ≤ i}`, `f(t) = min_{|C| = t} |N[C]|`\n699\t(`satisfiability/expansion_bound.py`; `EmptyPair.lean`,\n700\t`exists_closedNbhd_card_le` is its layout form), computed exactly by\n701\tbranch and bound up to a level cap and a time budget. Under a cap it is a\n702\t**lower bound on the true Harper value**, which is itself `≤ pw`. So, as\n703\t§8.5 (b) states it, `pw − Harper` as measured is an **upper** bound on\n704\tthe necessary condition's slack (the instance has empty pairs at `k`\n705\talthough `pw > k`) and `Harper − floor` a **lower** bound on the union\n706\tbound's. Where the forced prefix `t = ⌈(n − pw)/2⌉` exceeds the cap, the\n707\tinstrument does not reach the forced pair and both statements hold with\n708\troom (§11.4).\n709\t\n710\tTwo reads of the same ledger: the floors of the *counts* are model\n711\tstatements (a bound on `P(pw ≤ k)` over the generator, evaluated at the\n712\tinstance's sizes) and the two *deterministic* rungs (Harper, `pw`) are\n713\tinstance statements; a count's floor above an instance's `pw` is a\n714\tmodel event of probability at most `θ`, not a contradiction, and at\n715\t`< 0.01` on certified instances it is the stop condition of `TASK.md`.\n716\t\n717\t### 11.2 Covers: the 600 certified `(6, 1)` instances at `n = m = 30–75`\n718\t\n719\tThe fixed generator's `(6, 1)` instances of `learning/data/ensemble/\n720\tresults.csv` and `results_upward.csv` (`generator = fixed`, `param = 6`,\n721\t`m = n`, `n ≥ 30`; every one `certified`), whose Harper values are on\n722\trecord in `reports/scratch/structured_count/slack_6_1.csv` (`max_t = 12`,\n723\t60 s, §8.5 (b) of `excess_phase_diagram.md`; read here, never re-run) —\n724\t**600 instances, not the 650 the item and the plan say** (150 at each of\n725\t30, 35, 40 and 50 at each of 50, 60, 75; the record's own table sums to\n726\t600). Pattern sizes regenerated from the seeds (`learning.ensemble.generate`;\n727\tthe regenerated old and exact-size floors equal the record's `floor_old*`,\n728\t`floor_1*` on all 600, asserted); the closed-pair floor is the NA/tangent\n729\tbound of §7.1 (a′), the flip floor the exact weighted count of §7.1 (b),\n730\tboth scanned over `k` from five below the exact-size floor to past `pw`.\n731\tFloors at `< 0.01` on the `pw` scale; means per `n`, then the consecutive\n732\tdifferences as quantiles 10 / 50 / 90 with the mean in brackets\n733\t(`ledger_6_1.csv`, `summary.csv`, `run.log`):\n734\t\n735\t| `n` | `N` | old | exact-size | closed | flip | best | Harper | `pw` | exact − old | best − exact | Harper − best | `pw` − Harper | `pw` − best | union-bound share |\n736\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n737\t| 30 | 150 | 16.00 | 17.00 | 17.00 | 17.00 | 17.00 | 20.03 | 20.46 | 1.00 | 0.00 | 2 / 3 / 4 (3.03) | 0 / 0 / 1 (0.43) | 2 / 3 / 4 (3.46) | 0.88 |\n738\t| 35 | 150 | 19.00 | 20.00 | 20.00 | 20.00 | 20.00 | 22.87 | 23.27 | 1.00 | 0.00 | 2 / 3 / 4 (2.87) | 0 / 0 / 1 (0.40) | 2 / 3 / 4 (3.27) | 0.88 |\n739\t| 40 | 150 | 22.00 | 22.00 | 23.00 | 22.00 | 23.00 | 25.78 | 26.21 | 0.00 | 1.00 | 2 / 3 / 4 (2.78) | 0 / 0 / 1 (0.43) | 2 / 3 / 4 (3.21) | 0.87 |\n740\t| 50 | 50 | 26.12 | 27.06 | 28.00 | 28.00 | 28.00 | 31.26 | 31.92 | 0.94 | 0.94 | 2 / 3 / 5 (3.26) | 0 / 1 / 1 (0.66) | 3 / 4 / 5 (3.92) | 0.83 |\n741\t| 60 | 50 | 32.00 | 33.00 | 33.00 | 33.00 | 33.00 | 37.20 | 37.80 | 1.00 | 0.00 | 2 / 4 / 6 (4.20) | 0 / 1 / 1 (0.60) | 3 / 5 / 6 (4.80) | 0.88 |\n742\t| 75 | 50 | 39.36 | 40.18 | 41.00 | 40.18 | 41.00 | 45.16 | 46.40 | 0.82 | 0.82 | 2 / 4 / 6 (4.16) | 0 / 1 / 2 (1.24) | 4 / 6 / 7 (5.40) | 0.77 |\n743\t\n744\t(\"union-bound share\" is `Σ(Harper − best) / Σ(pw − best)` over the\n745\tinstances of the row: the part of the leftover that is *at least* the\n746\tunion bound's. The `< 1` table is in `run.log`.)\n747\t\n748\t* **The exact-size pair buys one stack over the old pair** (`|R| = N − t`\n749\t  against `t − 1`) at every size but 40, where the two round to the same\n750\t  floor; in decades at `k = pw` the exact-size count is 0.4–0.5 below the\n751\t  old one (mean `log₁₀` at `pw`: old `+2.38 … +5.35`, exact-size\n752\t  `+1.99 … +4.83` from `n = 30` to 75; `run.log`).\n753\t* **The closed count buys one more stack on half the sizes and nothing on\n754\t  the other half**: higher than the exact-size floor on 150 / 150 at\n755\t  `n = 40`, 47 / 50 at 50, 41 / 50 at 75, on none at 30, 35, 60, lower on\n756\t  none. In decades it is uniformly 0.5–1.4 below the exact-size count at\n757\t  `k = pw` (`+1.53 … +3.47`), which is §7.2's `+0.011` in `β` — `0.3–0.8`\n758\t  stacks at these `n`, rounding to one stack or to none by the parity of\n759\t  the floor.\n760\t* **The flips buy nothing on `(6, 1)`**: equal to the exact-size floor on\n761\t  every instance except the 47 at `n = 50` where both it and the closed\n762\t  count cross the same threshold; `0.03` decades below the exact-size\n763\t  count at `k = pw`; never above the closed count. Item 07 priced the\n764\t  flips at `0.001–0.006` in `β` at `μ = 1`, `d ≥ 4` (§7.2): `0.1–0.4`\n765\t  stacks here, invisible.\n766\t* **Harper is 2–6 stacks above the best count and 0–2 below `pw`.**\n767\t  `Harper − best`: median 3 at `n = 30–50`, 4 at 60–75, mean `2.8 → 4.2`;\n768\t  `pw − Harper`: median 0 at 30–40, 1 at 50–75, mean `0.40 → 1.24`\n769\t  (`Harper = pw` on 87–91 of 150 at 30–40, on 19–22 of 50 at 50–60, on 6\n770\t  of 50 at 75, where the cap binds, §11.4). Harper is at or above the best\n771\t  count on all 600.\n772\t* **Where the leftover sits**: of the `3.5 → 5.4` stacks between the best\n773\t  count's floor and `pw`, **at least 77–88% is the union bound** (Harper\n774\t  above the floor) and **at most 12–23% the necessary condition** (`pw`\n775\t  above Harper), and the second figure is inflated by the cap from\n776\t  `n = 50` on. The leftover grows with `n` in stacks (`3.5, 3.3, 3.2,\n777\t  3.9, 4.8, 5.4`) and shrinks as a fraction of `n` (`0.115 → 0.072`).\n778\t* **Violations.** At `< 0.01`: **zero, for every count, on all 600**; the\n779\t  stop condition of `TASK.md` did not fire. At `< 1` (a 99%-failure\n780\t  statement): exact-size 1, closed 4, flip 1, old 0 — what such a\n781\t  statement is allowed to do (§7.5 saw the same on the Chu & Stuckey\n782\t  files).\n783\t\n784\t### 11.3 `G(n, 10/n)`: the pilot's four cells at `n = 30, 40, 50, 60`\n785\t\n786\tThe pilot's `c = 10` graphs with a proof (`status ≠ upper`; 137, 137, 136,\n787\t133 — all of them, 38 by a minor certificate), regenerated from their\n788\tseeds by the pilot's own generator (`networkx.gnp_random_graph(n, 10/n,\n789\tseed)`; edge counts asserted against the record) with the recorded layout\n790\tre-checked: **543 of 543 layouts have the proved width in one of the two\n791\torientations** (`layout_vertex_separation`). The four count rungs are\n792\tcell quantities (`cells_gnp.csv`: the old pair, the exact-size pair, the\n793\tseparator count `C(n, k) P_N(E_bip)` with `P_N(E_bip)` exact by item 05's\n794\tpartition recursion, and item 06's closed count, for every `k`); Harper\n795\tis per graph, `harper_bound_graph` with 16 levels requested under 60 s\n796\t(§11.4 for what that bought). Floors at `< 0.01`, `pw` scale\n797\t(`ledger_gnp.csv`, `summary.csv`):\n798\t\n799\t| `n` | `N` | old | exact-size | separator | closed | best | Harper | `pw` (min / mean / max) | exact − old | best − exact | Harper − best | `pw` − Harper | `pw` − best | union-bound share | Harper = `pw` |\n800\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n801\t| 30 | 137 | 12 | 12 | 12 | 12 | 12 | 15.13 | 13 / 15.47 / 18 | 0 | 0 | 2 / 3 / 4 (3.13) | 0 / 0 / 1 (0.34) | 2 / 3 / 5 (3.47) | 0.90 | 91 |\n802\t| 40 | 137 | 16 | 16 | 16 | 16 | 16 | 19.40 | 17 / 19.72 / 23 | 0 | 0 | 2 / 3 / 5 (3.40) | 0 / 0 / 1 (0.31) | 2 / 4 / 5 (3.72) | 0.92 | 95 |\n803\t| 50 | 136 | 18 | 19 | 19 | 19 | 19 | 23.42 | 21 / 23.74 / 27 | 1 | 0 | 3 / 4 / 6 (4.42) | 0 / 0 / 1 (0.32) | 3 / 5 / 6 (4.74) | 0.93 | 92 |\n804\t| 60 | 133 | 22 | 22 | 23 | 23 | 23 | 26.26