.760) at every `c` from 2 to about 32, and within a\n71-factor 1.6–1.85 of the fitted slopes. On the clique-cover cells of\n--\n104-| 15 | Kneis, Mölle, Richter & Rossmanith 2009, *SIAM J. Discrete Math.* 23(1):407–427, DOI 10.1137/080715482 | every graph | `pw ≤ m/5.769 + O(log n)`; `m/5.217 + 3` with all bags sharing a large common set (abstract, read through Crossref; `13/75 = 1/5.769` confirmed by 17 p. 19) | 0.260 / 0.520 / 0.867; cubic 0.260 | no (closed) | [pub, abstract] |\n105-| 16 | Fomin, Gaspers, Saurabh & Stepanov 2009, *Algorithmica* 54:181–207, DOI 10.1007/s00453-007-9133-3 | every graph, `n > n_ε` | Lemma 1 **`pw ≤ n₃/6 + n₄/3 + 13n₅/30 + 23n₆/45 + n_{≥7} + εn`** (preprint p. 5; the survey's `n_{≥6}` was wrong); Lemma 2 `tw ≤ (m − n)/3 + εn` for connected `G` with `m/n ∈ [1.5, 2]` | 0.196 / 0.605 / 0.926; cubic 1/6 | yes | [pub] |\n106:| 17 | Edwards & McDermid 2015, *Algorithmica* 72(4):940–968, DOI 10.1007/s00453-014-9883-7 | every graph | Cor 5.2 **`pw(G) ≤ Σ_{d ≥ 3} g_{1/6}(d) n_d + o(n)`**, `g_{1/6}(2) = 0`, `g_{1/6}(3) = 1/6`, `n g(n) = (n − 2) g(n − 1) + g(n − 2) + 1`; Thm 5.3 for average degree `d` (connected or `d ≥ 5`) `pw ≤ (g_{1/6}(d) + o(1)) n = (1 − (7/2)/(d + 1) + O(d^{−3})) n`; restates Golovnev–Kutzkov: `pw ≤ (1 − 4ε ln d / d) n` for `d_ε ≤ d ≤ n/(1 + ε)` (pp. 19–20, 6) | **0.183 / 0.458 / 0.656**; cubic 1/6 | fetched (accepted manuscript) | [pub] |\n107-| 18 | Golovnev & Kutzkov 2014, *TCS* 526:18–27, DOI 10.1016/j.tcs.2014.01.010 | every graph of average degree `d ≥ d_ε` | as restated in 17: `pw ≤ (1 − 4ε ln d / d) n`, `d_ε = O(exp(1/ε))` | large `c` only | no | [pub, as restated] |\n108-| 19 | Díaz, Penrose, Petit & Serna 2001, *J. Algorithms* 39:78–116, DOI 10.1006/jagm.2000.1149; read in Petit's thesis (UPC 2001, ALCOM-FT TR-01-157) | RGG, `n` uniform points in `[0, 1]²`, radius `r_n → 0`, `n r_n² / log n → ∞` | thesis Thm 5.13: **`minvs(G_n) / (n r_n) → 1` a.s.**, likewise bandwidth and vertex bisection; Thm 5.10 `minvs ≥ (1 − 