{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011Cgd3X8UkZEHk6B47gNkQG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01STENxjucaL31Sd5cS78U7N","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/sec0.md <<'EOF'\n## 0. Summary: what counting events bought, and what it did not (item 12, 2026-11-01)\n\n**The question.** The first-moment lower bound on the pathwidth of `G(n, c/n)`\nand on the optimum of random MOSP instances (`β*(c)`, `β*(d, μ)`;\n`FirstMoment.lean`, `CliqueCoverMoment.lean`) counts *witnesses* — ordered\nempty pairs `(A, R)` at the forced sizes — and misses the fitted slopes by\n`0.08–0.10` in `β` on `G(n, c/n)` and `0.04–0.06` on covers. loop0010 located\nthe slack in the union bound over clustered witnesses. This loop asked whether\ncounting the **event** a narrow layout forces — once per separator, once per\nclosed pair, or with a weight that divides each witness by the size of its\ncluster — moves the constant, and by how much, and where.\n\n**The answer in one paragraph.** Three new first moments are valid and two\nare theorems in finite form (one in Lean). None moves the headline constants\nby the `0.02` the brief set as worth a page: on `G(n, c/n)` the separator\ncount gains `+0.011` at `c = 6` and `+0.004` at `c = 10`, the closed-pair count\n`+0.010` and `+0.008`; on random covers the closed-pair count gains `+0.011`\nat `(d, μ) = (4, 1)` and `(6, 1)`. **The route is closed for the headline\nconstants**, as the plan's pre-registered estimates said it would be. What it\nbought instead: a near-threshold gain (`+0.029` at `c = 3`, a third of the gap\nto the fitted slope), the method's threshold moved from `4 ln 2` to `2 ln 2`\nconditional on a cited large-deviation principle, a provable sandwich with the\npublished upper line of Edwards & McDermid (2015), a direct measurement of\nwhat the cluster of witnesses is (two lobes through the separator; on covers\nthe reversed pair and nothing else, so loop0010's `e^{0.23 n}` is a\nrare-instance artefact there), the whole union-bound slack as a bounded\nplanted statistic (`0.012–0.019` in `β` at `n ≤ 32`), and a ledger in stacks\non 1,143 certified instances. The literature search found the separator as the\nobject of a width first moment once (Do, Erde & Kang 2024, with a\ndeterministic inner bound) and the inner rate in a different literature\n(O'Connell 1998); we found no prior statement of the inner probability of the\nbipartition event, nor of its use for a width constant.\n\n### 0.1 The three events, and the weighted identity\n\nWith `k < n`, `N = n − k`, `t = ⌈N/2⌉`, `r = N − t`, a layout of vertex\nseparation `≤ k` gives at the prefix of size `t` three disjoint sets\n`A ∪ R ∪ S = V`, `|A| = t`, `|R| = r`, `|S| = k`, with no `A–R` edge (L1, §2.1;\nLean `exists_balanced_separator`). Three events, three counts:\n\n| count | what is counted | one event per |\n|---|---|---|\n| **pair** (on record) | `X` = ordered exact-size empty pairs `(A, R)` | witness |\n| **separator** | `k`-sets `S` with `E_bip(S)`: the components of `G − S` can be grouped into sides of sizes `t`, `r` (`E_relax`: no component larger than `t`; strictly weaker, `3K₂`) | separator |\n| **closed pair** | pairs with `S = N(A) ∩ N(R)`, sides at least the forced sizes, `|S| ≤ k`; the fixpoint of one round of `R* = V ∖ N[A]`, `A* = V ∖ N[R*]` | closed pair |\n| **weighted** | `Y = Σ_P 1[P empty]/Z(P)` for any `1 ≤ Z ≤ X` on the empty pairs; `Y ≥ 1[X > 0]` pointwise, `= 1[X > 0]` at `Z = X` | cluster (as `Z` sees it) |\n\n\"An exact-size pair exists\" and \"some `k`-set is in `E_bip`\" are the same\nevent, counted differently (L1′ c). Two identities carry the measurements:\n`E[X′ | P₀ empty] = E[X²]/E[X] − 1` (the second-moment ratio *is* the planted\nmean) and `P(X > 0)/E[X] = E[1/X | P₀ empty]` (the union bound's whole slack is\na bounded planted statistic).\n\n### 0.2 The ladder, with the status of each rung\n\n| rung | theorem (Lean name) | on paper | measured (size range; section) | fitted | conditional / conjectured |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| L1, L1′ (a, b, d), L2, L3: the structures a narrow layout forces | `exists_balanced_separator`, `exists_balanced_separator_cover`, `exists_isBalancedBip`, `card_componentOff_le_of_isBalancedBip`, `closeStep_isClosedPair`, `closeStep_closeStep`, `exists_closedPair_of_pathwidth_le`, `isClosedPair_iff_sees_both`, … (30 names, §10.1) | L1′ (c) converse, §2.2 | checked on every graph to 9 vertices, 20,000 random at 10–12, 2,000 covers: zero violations (§2.4) | — | — |\n| exact-size pair count | the `Z ≡ 1` instance of `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_weighted` | §8.1 | floors on 200 Chu & Stuckey and 1,143 certified instances (§7.5, §11) | — | — |\n| **Theorem S** (separator count, finite form) | `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_choose_mul_innerBip` (inner probability as a weighted count; relabelling `innerBip_eq_of_card_eq`) | the inner probability by the partition formula (Lemma P) and Gilbert's recursion (Lemmas G, F), §8.1–§8.2; exact to `N = 120` (`E_bip`), `N = 400` (`E_relax`), §5 | `n = 60, 120`, `c = 3–10` in stacks (§5.2, §6.5, §9.6) | the rate of `E_bip` beyond `N = 120`; `β_sep(fitted)` (§6.1) | `β_sep(cited)` rests on the LDP for the largest component (O'Connell 1998 via Puhalskii 2005 Cor. 2.4(3)); `E_bip` and `E_relax` of equal rate beyond `N = 120` (§5.3) |\n| **Theorem Cl** (closed-pair count) | union bound `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_sum_closedPairs`; characterisation `isClosedPair_iff_sees_both` | the independence step and the exact expectation, §8.1; `β_closed` the root of a closed-form exponent, §6.1 (b) | floors (§6.5, §7.5, §11) | — | the supremum at the corner at every `c` (numerical, ten `c`) |\n| Theorem Cl-cover, the NA bound | — | the `(u, w)` inclusion–exclusion, §7.1 (a); the cancellation-free bound by negative association (Joag-Dev & Proschan 1983, cited), §7.1 (a′) | exact against enumeration at `n ≤ 8`; the NA bound's slack a constant `0.2` nats at `n = 8–26` (§7.3) | the NA bound's slope | — |\n| **Lemma W** (weighted count), Lemma Fl (flips), Corollary W-flip | `weightedCount_ge_indicator`, `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_weighted`, `flipPair_*`, `card_flips_le`, `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_flipWeighted` | Lemma J (joint binomial moments), the evaluation of `E[Y]`, §8.1 | `E[Y]` within 1.7 s.e. of 1,000 Monte Carlo covers (§8.3) | — | — |\n| Lemma Rc (recombinations), `Ẑ₀`, `β_W` | — | §9.1, §9.3 (the transform of `Ẑ₀` a binomial sum) | every labelled graph to 6 vertices; planted lower tail at `n ≤ 32` (§9.2) | — | — |\n| the combined count | — | §6.1 (c), valid, not the best | — | fitted only (no LDP for the tilted event) | — |\n| Harper (the necessary condition's instrument) | `exists_closedNbhd_card_le` (`EmptyPair.lean`) | — | 1,143 instances under a level cap and a budget (§11) | — | — |\n| Proposition T (threshold `2 ln 2`), T-cover (half-giant line) | — | §6.4, §7.4, §8.1 | `N ≤ 400` consistent at `c = 2, 2.5`, undecided at `1.5` (§6.4) | — | (H_G) cited, not verified by us; (H_C) stated in no held paper |\n\nEvery Lean theorem of the loop is in `lean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean`\n(78 theorems, 21 definitions; no `sorry`, no `axiom`; `propext`,\n`Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound` only, `paper1/axiom_check.lean`); what is on\npaper and not in Lean is named with its obstacle in §10.3 (components of\n`G − S` as finsets; the product-over-blocks lemma; inclusion–exclusion over\npattern sets).\n\n### 0.3 The constants\n\n`G(n, c/n)` (§6.3, §9.3, §9.6; `constants.csv`, `beta_w.csv`,\n`threshold_fine.csv`). `β_sep` (cited) is the root of\n`H(β) = (1 − β) I(c(1 − β))` with `I` the LDP rate of O'Connell as restated by\nPuhalskii, **cited**; `β_sep` (fitted) uses the log-corrected fit of the exact\n`−log P_N(E_relax)` over `N = 100–400`, **fitted**; `β_closed` and `β_W` are\nroots of closed-form exponents (on paper, the supremum located numerically);\nthe slope is the pilot's fitted `β_∞` (survey §7(d), `n ≤ 70–120`,\n**fitted**); E&M is Edwards & McDermid (2015) Cor. 5.2 on Poisson(`c`)\ndegrees, the published upper line (owner's note).\n\n| `c` | `β*` | `β_sep` cited | `β_sep` fitted | `β_closed` | `β_W` (`Ẑ₀`) | best valid | fitted slope | E&M upper | share of the gap closed |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2 | 0 | 0.0056 | 0.0059 | 0 | 0 | 0.006 | 0.040 | 0.085 | 15% |\n| 2.8 | 0.0008 | 0.0290 | 0.0294 | 0.0008 | 0.0008 | 0.029 | — | 0.162 | — |\n| 3 | 0.0087 | 0.0368 | 0.0374 | 0.0096 | 0.0096 | 0.037 | 0.099 | 0.183 | 32% |\n| 4 | 0.0613 | 0.0827 | 0.0833 | 0.0671 | 0.0671 | 0.083 | 0.158 | 0.285 | 23% |\n| 6 | 0.1706 | 0.1817 | 0.1820 | 0.1803 | 0.1801 | 0.182 | 0.268 | 0.458 | 12% |\n| 8 | 0.2628 | 0.2690 | 0.2691 | 0.2722 | 0.2720 | 0.272 | 0.360 | 0.576 | 10% |\n| 10 | 0.3371 | 0.3409 | 0.3410 | 0.3453 | 0.3451 | 0.345 | 0.415 | 0.656 | 11% |\n| 20 | 0.5535 | 0.5542 | 0.5543 | 0.5573 | 0.5572 | 0.557 | — | 0.826 | — |\n\nThe separator count's gain is a sparse-side one and peaks in `β` at the pair\ncount's own threshold `c = 4 ln 2` (`+0.029`); the closed count's is a\ndense-side one (the `q` terms, `2β ln q((1 − β)/2)` nats) and wins from\n`c = 8`. The combined count (closed pairs grouped by separator with a `2^κ`\nbound on the colourings) is below the closed count everywhere and below `β*`\nat `c ≤ 4`. Conversion: the pair exponent's slope at `β*` is `5.5, 3.9, 3.4,\n3.3, 3.3` nats per unit of `β` at `c = 3, 4, 6, 8, 10`, so a gain of `g` nats\nper vertex is `g/3.3` in `β` at `c ≥ 6`.\n\nRandom clique covers (`m = μ n` patterns of `d` customers, the i.i.d. model of\n`CliqueCoverMoment.lean`; §7.2, `grid.csv`). `β_closed` by the valid\nnegative-association bound (the independent-sites approximation differs by\n`≤ 0.001`); `β_flip` the exact weighted count with the flip weight; `b` the\ncertified slope of `excess_phase_diagram.md` §2.5 (**measured**, 30–100\ncustomers); E&M on the cover degree law.\n\n| `(d, μ)` | `β*` | `β_closed` | `β_flip` | best | `b` | E&M upper | share of the gap |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| (4, 1) | 0.2859 | 0.2969 | 0.2917 | 0.297 | 0.348 | 0.660 | 18% |\n| (6, 1) | 0.5132 | 0.5244 | 0.5155 | 0.524 | 0.577 | 0.861 | 18% |\n| (10, 1) | 0.7567 | 0.7614 | 0.7570 | 0.761 | 0.795 | 0.957 | 12% |\n| (8, ½) | 0.3977 | 0.4188 | 0.4039 | 0.419 | 0.463 | 0.831 | 32% |\n| CS 125×125, `d = 2` (pooled sizes) | 0.0983 | 0.1039 | 0.1096 | 0.110 | 0.146 | 0.392 | 24% |\n| CS 125×125, `d = 4` | 0.3208 | 0.3345 | 0.3268 | 0.335 | 0.396 | 0.729 | 18% |\n\nThe separator count's constant is not computed on covers (no LDP to cite for\nthe giant of a random intersection graph); the closed count is a sparse-side\ngain there, largest at few large patterns (`+0.021` at `(8, ½)`, the one cell\nabove `0.02`, outside the kill's named cells); the flips are worth\n`0.001–0.006` at `μ ≥ 1`, `d ≥ 4` and `+0.011` at the Chu & Stuckey `d = 2`\nsizes. E&M is loose on covers (it sees the degrees of a union of cliques, not\nthe cliques); the project's own `β⁺` (`excess_phase_diagram.md` §7) is the\ntighter upper end there.\n\n### 0.4 The thresholds, with their hypotheses\n\n* **Proposition T** (§6.4, §8.1). *If* for every `c′ > 2 ln 2` there is\n  `I(c′) > 0`, continuous, with `P(no component of G(N, c′/N) exceeds N/2) ≤\n  e^{−(I(c′) − o(1)) N}`, *then* `β_sep(c) > 0` for every `c > 2 ln 2`. The\n  hypothesis is the upper-bound half of the LDP for the largest component on\n  the closed set `[0, ½]`: O'Connell 1998 (not held) as restated by\n  Puhalskii 2005 (Cor. 2.4(3), held) and Andreis–König–Patterson 2021\n  (Cor. 1.3, held); `I_{c′}(½) > 0` iff `c′ > 2 ln 2` on the quoted formula.\n  **Cited, not verified by us as a theorem.** What is verified: the value of\n  the quoted formula against the exact finite computation at seven `c′`\n  (`0.0003–0.002`, §5.3), and the finite rate bounded away from zero at\n  `c = 2, 2.5` to `N = 400`, undecided at `c = 1.5`. The method's threshold\n  was `4 ln 2 = 2.77`; this moves it to `2 ln 2 = 1.39`, the bisection\n  threshold of Luczak–McDiarmid for the same reason; the truth is `1`\n  (Lee–Lee–Oum 2012).\n* **Proposition T-cover** (§7.4). *If* the largest component of the MOSP\n  graph of a random cover has an exponentially small lower tail below its\n  typical fraction `θ(d, μ)`, *then* the separator count's floor is positive\n  wherever `θ > ½`. **The hypothesis is stated in no held paper** (Behrisch\n  2007 and Lagerås–Lindholm 2008 give the law of large numbers only). The\n  half-giant line `θ = ½` sits at excess `e = 0.595, 0.603, 0.658, 0.736,\n  0.816` for `μ = ⅛, ¼, ½, 1, 2`, between loop0010's `e_g(r)` and the pair\n  count's `e = 1`; the ensembles on record cannot confirm it (repaired and\n  connectivity-conditioned generators).\n\n### 0.5 The clumping, decomposed (items 03, 04, 09)\n\nOn instances with exact pathwidth at `n ≤ 24` and `k = pw`, a typical\ninstance has 8–62 exact-size empty pairs; one separator carries one pair and\nits reverse (`X₁/X₂ = 1.03–1.6` with `N` odd), the closure merges `1.3–1.6`\n(graphs) and `1.7–3.3` (covers), the single-swap classes `1.4–2.5`, and **no\nratio grows with `n`** (`0.000 ± 0.003` nats per vertex at `c = 10` against\nthe `0.066` a `0.02` gain needs). The second moment's `e^{0.23–0.39 n}` is a\nstatement about the rare-instance regime at `β*`, where the maximising\noverlap is the pair itself or its reverse perturbed through `S`, not the\nsymmetric table typical instances show. Planting a pair and enumerating the\nothers (`n ≤ 32`, 200 per cell) measures that regime directly: the cluster is\n**two lobes with an empty middle** (perturbations of `P₀` and of its reverse;\nthe moved separator vertices have half the planted-side degree of a typical\none and evict at most one neighbour in 60–87% of cases), the median cluster\ngrows at about half the mean's rate on `G(n, c/n)` (`0.24 ± 0.03` against\n`0.31 ± 0.03` nats per vertex at `c = 6`) and **not at all on `(6, 1)`\ncovers** (median `X′ = 1`, the reversed pair, at every size): loop0010's\n`e^{0.23 n}` is a rare-instance artefact of `E[X²]` there. The union bound's\nwhole slack, `−log E[1/X | P₀ empty]`, is `0.065, 0.039, 0.043` nats per\nvertex at the largest sizes (`0.019, 0.012, 0.015` in `β`), sub-linear in `n`\nover the range; the recombinations through the separator (Lemma Rc, `Z_4`)\nrecover 54%, 79% and 98% of it, the computable `Ẑ₀` a third, and the lower\ntail of every `Z` with a closed-form transform is the event *the planted pair\nis closed*, which is why `β_W = β_closed − 0.0002`.\n\n### 0.6 In stacks, on certified instances (item 11)\n\n600 certified `(6, 1)` covers at `n = m = 30–75` and 543 proved `G(n, 10/n)`\ngraphs at `n = 30–60`, floors at `< 0.01` on the `pw` scale, **zero floors\nabove a certified pathwidth for any count**. At `n = 75` on covers the old\npair's floor is 7.0 stacks below the pathwidth; exact sizes buy 0.8, the\nclosed count 0.8 more, the flips nothing: **1.6 of the seven**. At\n`G(60, 10/60)` the old floor is 5.8 below the mean pathwidth and the\nseparator and closed counts buy **one stack**, the same one. Of the 4.8–5.4\nstacks left, Harper's vertex-isoperimetric bound sits at or above the best\ncount on 1,142 of 1,143 instances and within a stack of the pathwidth\nwherever its branch and bound reaches the forced prefix (`n ≤ 40` on covers,\n`n ≤ 50` on graphs), so **at least 77–93% of the leftover is the union bound\nby that instrument** and at most a stack the necessary condition; at larger\n`n` the level cap binds and the split is the cap's (§11.5). This does not\nagree in size with §0.5's planted `0.012–0.019` in `β` (about one stack at\n`n = 75`): the two instruments see different sizes (`n ≤ 32` against 30–75)\nand different quantities (a planted mean against a deterministic bound at\n`θ = 0.01`), and the reconciliation is open (§0.9).\n\n### 0.7 Kill verdicts\n\n| item | criterion | verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| 01 literature | stop rule: a prior separator first moment with an exact inner probability for pathwidth of `G(n, c/n)` | **did not fire** |\n| 02 lemmas | a counterexample to L1, L1′, L2, L3 | **not met** (310,266 graphs, 4,027,298 closures, zero) |\n| 03 clumping | (1) `X₁/X₂`, `X₁/X₃` grow at `< 0.035` nats per vertex at `c = 10`; (2) `X₁/X₄` grows at `≥ 0.15` | (1) **met** (`0.000 ± 0.003`, `−0.003 ± 0.003`); (2) **not met** |\n| 04 planted | the fork: typical / in between / artefact | `G(n, c/n)`: in between (ratios 0.57, 0.36); covers: **artefact** (0) |\n| 05 inner | separator floor at most one stack over the pair floor at every pilot cell | **met for `c ≥ 6`** (all six cells); 2–3 stacks at `c = 3–4` |\n| 06 constants | `β_sep − β* < 0.02` at `c = 6, 10` | **met** (`+0.0113`, `+0.0038`); separate: `+0.029` at `c = 3`, threshold `2 ln 2` conditional |\n| 07 covers | `β_closed − β* < 0.02` at `(6, 1)`, `(4, 1)` | **met** (`+0.0111`, `+0.0110`); `(8, ½)` at `+0.0211` outside the named cells; zero floor violations on 200 |\n| 08 theorems | a counterexample at `n ≤ 7` | **not met** (zero violations in exact rationals) |\n| 09 weighted | a computable `Z` beating the closed count by `0.02` | **met** (`β_W − β_closed = −0.0002`) |\n| 10 Lean | none | everything of (a)–(d) proved; obstacles named |\n| 11 ledger | none; stop condition: a floor above a certified pathwidth | **did not fire** (1,143 instances) |\n| 12 write-up | none | — |\n\n### 0.8 What this is not\n\n* **Not a new headline constant.** `β_sep`, `β_closed`, `β_W` are valid lower\n  bounds on `lim inf pw/n` under the stated bases; none moves `β*` by `0.02`\n  at `c = 6, 10` or at `(4, 1), (6, 1)`; the gaps \"closed\" are fractions of\n  fitted slopes.\n* **Not a theorem about rates.** Theorem S and Theorem Cl are finite\n  inequalities; every rate is either cited (the LDP, not proved here) or\n  fitted (labelled). `E_bip = E_relax` in rate is exact to `N = 120` and\n  conjectural beyond. Propositions T and T-cover are conditional.\n* **Not asymptotic where it is measured.** The planted cluster is at\n  `n ≤ 32`, the ledger at 30–75, the clumping at `n ≤ 24`; the per-vertex\n  slacks are sub-linear over their ranges and are upper estimates of a rate.\n* **Not a priority claim.** The separator object is in Do–Erde–Kang 2024;\n  the inner rate is O'Connell's; the threshold `2 ln 2` is Luczak–McDiarmid's\n  bisection threshold; \"we found no prior statement\" is the wording.\n* **Not canonical.** The closure is a representative (the `A`-first and\n  `R`-first fixpoints differ on 3–14% of pairs); a union bound needs only a\n  map.\n* **Not re-solved.** No certified value was recomputed; `solutions/` was\n  not read; the only new exact solves are 4,800 fresh graphs at `n ≤ 24`\n  (item 03), layouts kept.\n\n### 0.9 Open\n\n1. **Theorem Cl into Lean**: the product-over-blocks lemma for weighted sums\n   over edge subsets (a session; §10.3). Lemmas P, G, F and Corollary S′ need\n   components of `G − S` as finsets; Lemma J and Theorem Cl-cover need\n   inclusion–exclusion over pattern sets.\n2. **The hypotheses.** (H_G): verify the quoted LDP statement against the\n   held sources in full (O'Connell 1998 is not held). (H_C): an exponentially\n   small lower tail for the giant of a random intersection graph, in no held\n   paper.\n3. **The two instruments.** The planted slack (`0.012–0.019` in `β` at\n   `n ≤ 32`) against the Harper ledger (three quarters of 4–5 stacks at\n   30–75): a Harper run with no level cap at `n = 60–75`, and the planted\n   measurement at `n = 48–64`, would say whether the union bound's slack\n   grows with `n` or the necessary condition's rounding is what the ledger\n   sees.\n4. **A count that merges both lobes.** `Z_4`'s transform (the two-sided and\n   reversed-lobe moves, which need the edge-free pairs inside `G[S]`) has no\n   closed form here and is worth twice `Ẑ₀` at `n = 32`; and a combined\n   count with the closedness condition inside the component law (not a\n   `2^κ` tilt).\n5. **Near the threshold.** `β_sep` at `c = 2–4` is the best lower bound on\n   record and the sandwich to E&M is `5–14×` wide; nothing exact is known\n   there, and the pilot has no fitted slope between `c = 2` and `3`.\n6. **The sparse cover cells.** The closed count passes `0.02` at `(8, ½)` and\n   the additive closed-plus-flip estimate passes it at `μ ≤ 1`, `d = 3–4`; no\n   single count realises both mechanisms.\n7. **The half-giant line on the i.i.d. model**, measured (the ensembles on\n   record are repaired or connectivity-conditioned).\n\n### 0.10 Where everything is\n\nSections 1–11 are the items in order, each with its question, its events,\nits size range, its regenerate command, its kill verdict and what it does not\nclaim. Code: `learning/separator_moment.py` (tested by\n`tests/test_separator_moment.py`, 91 tests); scratch, logs and CSVs under\n`reports/scratch/separator_moment/NN_*/`; Lean in\n`lean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean`; five papers added to\n`literature/` and five recorded missing in `literature/MISSING.md`; the paper's\nAppendix E (`paper1/latex/sec9e_appendix_random.tex`, the paragraph \"Why the\nfirst moment is loose\", the section's closing, five Appendix A rows and seven\nreferences with checked DOIs). Compute: about 8.5 core-hours in all against\n12 planned, 4.9 of them item 11's Harper pass. The paragraph the owner will\nneed for `CLAUDE.md` is the last section of this document.\n\n---\n\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"reports/separator_moment.md\")\ns = p.read_text()\nold_hdr = \"verdict and what it does not claim. §0 (the summary) is written by item\\n12.*\"\nassert s.count(old_hdr) == 1\ns = s.replace(old_hdr, \"verdict and what it does not claim. §0 is the summary (item 12); the\\nparagraph for `CLAUDE.md` is the last section.*\")\nanchor = \"\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Literature: who counts separators\"\nassert s.count(anchor) == 1\nsec0 = Path(\"/tmp/sec0.md\").read_text()\ns = s.replace(anchor, \"\\n---\\n\\n\" + sec0 + \"## 1. Literature: who counts separators\")\np.write_text(s)\nprint(\"inserted\", len(s.splitlines()))\nPYEOF\ngrep -n '^## ' reports/separator_moment.md | head -5","description":"Insert the summary section §0 into the report and update its header"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":573,"cache_read_input_tokens":341239,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":573,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"705e2dc1-3bd5-4ca7-a2e8-b0a1809ff2f3","uuid":"09e6a7a5-e126-4a0e-9453-8de712633513","timestamp":"2026-11-01T23:06:58.094Z","request_id":"req_011Cgd3X84hg43rnEiskPz4h","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01STENxjucaL31Sd5cS78U7N":{"command":"cd /home/al/dev/MOSP && cat > /tmp/sec0.md <<'EOF'\n## 0. Summary: what counting events bought, and what it did not (item 12, 2026-11-01)\n\n**The question.** The first-moment lower bound on the pathwidth of `G(n, c/n)`\nand on the optimum of random MOSP instances (`β*(c)`, `β*(d, μ)`;\n`FirstMoment.lean`, `CliqueCoverMoment.lean`) counts *witnesses* — ordered\nempty pairs `(A, R)` at the forced sizes — and misses the fitted slopes by\n`0.08–0.10` in `β` on `G(n, c/n)` and `0.04–0.06` on covers. loop0010 located\nthe slack in the union bound over clustered witnesses. This loop asked whether\ncounting the **event** a narrow layout forces — once per separator, once per\nclosed pair, or with a weight that divides each witness by the size of its\ncluster — moves the constant, and by how much, and where.\n\n**The answer in one paragraph.** Three new first moments are valid and two\nare theorems in finite form (one in Lean). None moves the headline constants\nby the `0.02` the brief set as worth a page: on `G(n, c/n)` the separator\ncount gains `+0.011` at `c = 6` and `+0.004` at `c = 10`, the closed-pair count\n`+0.010` and `+0.008`; on random covers the closed-pair count gains `+0.011`\nat `(d, μ) = (4, 1)` and `(6, 1)`. **The route is closed for the headline\nconstants**, as the plan's pre-registered estimates said it would be. What it\nbought instead: a near-threshold gain (`+0.029` at `c = 3`, a third of the gap\nto the fitted slope), the method's threshold moved from `4 ln 2` to `2 ln 2`\nconditional on a cited large-deviation principle, a provable sandwich with the\npublished upper line of Edwards & McDermid (2015), a direct measurement of\nwhat the cluster of witnesses is (two lobes through the separator; on covers\nthe reversed pair and nothing else, so loop0010's `e^{0.23 n}` is a\nrare-instance artefact there), the whole union-bound slack as a bounded\nplanted statistic (`0.012–0.019` in `β` at `n ≤ 32`), and a ledger in stacks\non 1,143 certified instances. The literature search found the separator as the\nobject of a width first moment once (Do, Erde & Kang 2024, with a\ndeterministic inner bound) and the inner rate in a different literature\n(O'Connell 1998); we found no prior statement of the inner probability of the\nbipartition event, nor of its use for a width constant.\n\n### 0.1 The three events, and the weighted identity\n\nWith `k < n`, `N = n − k`, `t = ⌈N/2⌉`, `r = N − t`, a layout of vertex\nseparation `≤ k` gives at the prefix of size `t` three disjoint sets\n`A ∪ R ∪ S = V`, `|A| = t`, `|R| = r`, `|S| = k`, with no `A–R` edge (L1, §2.1;\nLean `exists_balanced_separator`). Three events, three counts:\n\n| count | what is counted | one event per |\n|---|---|---|\n| **pair** (on record) | `X` = ordered exact-size empty pairs `(A, R)` | witness |\n| **separator** | `k`-sets `S` with `E_bip(S)`: the components of `G − S` can be grouped into sides of sizes `t`, `r` (`E_relax`: no component larger than `t`; strictly weaker, `3K₂`) | separator |\n| **closed pair** | pairs with `S = N(A) ∩ N(R)`, sides at least the forced sizes, `|S| ≤ k`; the fixpoint of one round of `R* = V ∖ N[A]`, `A* = V ∖ N[R*]` | closed pair |\n| **weighted** | `Y = Σ_P 1[P empty]/Z(P)` for any `1 ≤ Z ≤ X` on the empty pairs; `Y ≥ 1[X > 0]` pointwise, `= 1[X > 0]` at `Z = X` | cluster (as `Z` sees it) |\n\n\"An exact-size pair exists\" and \"some `k`-set is in `E_bip`\" are the same\nevent, counted differently (L1′ c). Two identities carry the measurements:\n`E[X′ | P₀ empty] = E[X²]/E[X] − 1` (the second-moment ratio *is* the planted\nmean) and `P(X > 0)/E[X] = E[1/X | P₀ empty]` (the union bound's whole slack is\na bounded planted statistic).\n\n### 0.2 The ladder, with the status of each rung\n\n| rung | theorem (Lean name) | on paper | measured (size range; section) | fitted | conditional / conjectured |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| L1, L1′ (a, b, d), L2, L3: the structures a narrow layout forces | `exists_balanced_separator`, `exists_balanced_separator_cover`, `exists_isBalancedBip`, `card_componentOff_le_of_isBalancedBip`, `closeStep_isClosedPair`, `closeStep_closeStep`, `exists_closedPair_of_pathwidth_le`, `isClosedPair_iff_sees_both`, … (30 names, §10.1) | L1′ (c) converse, §2.2 | checked on every graph to 9 vertices, 20,000 random at 10–12, 2,000 covers: zero violations (§2.4) | — | — |\n| exact-size pair count | the `Z ≡ 1` instance of `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_weighted` | §8.1 | floors on 200 Chu & Stuckey and 1,143 certified instances (§7.5, §11) | — | — |\n| **Theorem S** (separator count, finite form) | `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_choose_mul_innerBip` (inner probability as a weighted count; relabelling `innerBip_eq_of_card_eq`) | the inner probability by the partition formula (Lemma P) and Gilbert's recursion (Lemmas G, F), §8.1–§8.2; exact to `N = 120` (`E_bip`), `N = 400` (`E_relax`), §5 | `n = 60, 120`, `c = 3–10` in stacks (§5.2, §6.5, §9.6) | the rate of `E_bip` beyond `N = 120`; `β_sep(fitted)` (§6.1) | `β_sep(cited)` rests on the LDP for the largest component (O'Connell 1998 via Puhalskii 2005 Cor. 2.4(3)); `E_bip` and `E_relax` of equal rate beyond `N = 120` (§5.3) |\n| **Theorem Cl** (closed-pair count) | union bound `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_sum_closedPairs`; characterisation `isClosedPair_iff_sees_both` | the independence step and the exact expectation, §8.1; `β_closed` the root of a closed-form exponent, §6.1 (b) | floors (§6.5, §7.5, §11) | — | the supremum at the corner at every `c` (numerical, ten `c`) |\n| Theorem Cl-cover, the NA bound | — | the `(u, w)` inclusion–exclusion, §7.1 (a); the cancellation-free bound by negative association (Joag-Dev & Proschan 1983, cited), §7.1 (a′) | exact against enumeration at `n ≤ 8`; the NA bound's slack a constant `0.2` nats at `n = 8–26` (§7.3) | the NA bound's slope | — |\n| **Lemma W** (weighted count), Lemma Fl (flips), Corollary W-flip | `weightedCount_ge_indicator`, `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_weighted`, `flipPair_*`, `card_flips_le`, `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_flipWeighted` | Lemma J (joint binomial moments), the evaluation of `E[Y]`, §8.1 | `E[Y]` within 1.7 s.e. of 1,000 Monte Carlo covers (§8.3) | — | — |\n| Lemma Rc (recombinations), `Ẑ₀`, `β_W` | — | §9.1, §9.3 (the transform of `Ẑ₀` a binomial sum) | every labelled graph to 6 vertices; planted lower tail at `n ≤ 32` (§9.2) | — | — |\n| the combined count | — | §6.1 (c), valid, not the best | — | fitted only (no LDP for the tilted event) | — |\n| Harper (the necessary condition's instrument) | `exists_closedNbhd_card_le` (`EmptyPair.lean`) | — | 1,143 instances under a level cap and a budget (§11) | — | — |\n| Proposition T (threshold `2 ln 2`), T-cover (half-giant line) | — | §6.4, §7.4, §8.1 | `N ≤ 400` consistent at `c = 2, 2.5`, undecided at `1.5` (§6.4) | — | (H_G) cited, not verified by us; (H_C) stated in no held paper |\n\nEvery Lean theorem of the loop is in `lean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean`\n(78 theorems, 21 definitions; no `sorry`, no `axiom`; `propext`,\n`Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound` only, `paper1/axiom_check.lean`); what is on\npaper and not in Lean is named with its obstacle in §10.3 (components of\n`G − S` as finsets; the product-over-blocks lemma; inclusion–exclusion over\npattern sets).\n\n### 0.3 The constants\n\n`G(n, c/n)` (§6.3, §9.3, §9.6; `constants.csv`, `beta_w.csv`,\n`threshold_fine.csv`). `β_sep` (cited) is the root of\n`H(β) = (1 − β) I(c(1 − β))` with `I` the LDP rate of O'Connell as restated by\nPuhalskii, **cited**; `β_sep` (fitted) uses the log-corrected fit of the exact\n`−log P_N(E_relax)` over `N = 100–400`, **fitted**; `β_closed` and `β_W` are\nroots of closed-form exponents (on paper, the supremum located numerically);\nthe slope is the pilot's fitted `β_∞` (survey §7(d), `n ≤ 70–120`,\n**fitted**); E&M is Edwards & McDermid (2015) Cor. 5.2 on Poisson(`c`)\ndegrees, the published upper line (owner's note).\n\n| `c` | `β*` | `β_sep` cited | `β_sep` fitted | `β_closed` | `β_W` (`Ẑ₀`) | best valid | fitted slope | E&M upper | share of the gap closed |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2 | 0 | 0.0056 | 0.0059 | 0 | 0 | 0.006 | 0.040 | 0.085 | 15% |\n| 2.8 | 0.0008 | 0.0290 | 0.0294 | 0.0008 | 0.0008 | 0.029 | — | 0.162 | — |\n| 3 | 0.0087 | 0.0368 | 0.0374 | 0.0096 | 0.0096 | 0.037 | 0.099 | 0.183 | 32% |\n| 4 | 0.0613 | 0.0827 | 0.0833 | 0.0671 | 0.0671 | 0.083 | 0.158 | 0.285 | 23% |\n| 6 | 0.1706 | 0.1817 | 0.1820 | 0.1803 | 0.1801 | 0.182 | 0.268 | 0.458 | 12% |\n| 8 | 0.2628 | 0.2690 | 0.2691 | 0.2722 | 0.2720 | 0.272 | 0.360 | 0.576 | 10% |\n| 10 | 0.3371 | 0.3409 | 0.3410 | 0.3453 | 0.3451 | 0.345 | 0.415 | 0.656 | 11% |\n| 20 | 0.5535 | 0.5542 | 0.5543 | 0.5573 | 0.5572 | 0.557 | — | 0.826 | — |\n\nThe separator count's gain is a sparse-side one and peaks in `β` at the pair\ncount's own threshold `c = 4 ln 2` (`+0.029`); the closed count's is a\ndense-side one (the `q` terms, `2β ln q((1 − β)/2)` nats) and wins from\n`c = 8`. The combined count (closed pairs grouped by separator with a `2^κ`\nbound on the colourings) is below the closed count everywhere and below `β*`\nat `c ≤ 4`. Conversion: the pair exponent's slope at `β*` is `5.5, 3.9, 3.4,\n3.3, 3.3` nats per unit of `β` at `c = 3, 4, 6, 8, 10`, so a gain of `g` nats\nper vertex is `g/3.3` in `β` at `c ≥ 6`.\n\nRandom clique covers (`m = μ n` patterns of `d` customers, the i.i.d. model of\n`CliqueCoverMoment.lean`; §7.2, `grid.csv`). `β_closed` by the valid\nnegative-association bound (the independent-sites approximation differs by\n`≤ 0.001`); `β_flip` the exact weighted count with the flip weight; `b` the\ncertified slope of `excess_phase_diagram.md` §2.5 (**measured**, 30–100\ncustomers); E&M on the cover degree law.\n\n| `(d, μ)` | `β*` | `β_closed` | `β_flip` | best | `b` | E&M upper | share of the gap |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| (4, 1) | 0.2859 | 0.2969 | 0.2917 | 0.297 | 0.348 | 0.660 | 18% |\n| (6, 1) | 0.5132 | 0.5244 | 0.5155 | 0.524 | 0.577 | 0.861 | 18% |\n| (10, 1) | 0.7567 | 0.7614 | 0.7570 | 0.761 | 0.795 | 0.957 | 12% |\n| (8, ½) | 0.3977 | 0.4188 | 0.4039 | 0.419 | 0.463 | 0.831 | 32% |\n| CS 125×125, `d = 2` (pooled sizes) | 0.0983 | 0.1039 | 0.1096 | 0.110 | 0.146 | 0.392 | 24% |\n| CS 125×125, `d = 4` | 0.3208 | 0.3345 | 0.3268 | 0.335 | 0.396 | 0.729 | 18% |\n\nThe separator count's constant is not computed on covers (no LDP to cite for\nthe giant of a random intersection graph); the closed count is a sparse-side\ngain there, largest at few large patterns (`+0.021` at `(8, ½)`, the one cell\nabove `0.02`, outside the kill's named cells); the flips are worth\n`0.001–0.006` at `μ ≥ 1`, `d ≥ 4` and `+0.011` at the Chu & Stuckey `d = 2`\nsizes. E&M is loose on covers (it sees the degrees of a union of cliques, not\nthe cliques); the project's own `β⁺` (`excess_phase_diagram.md` §7) is the\ntighter upper end there.\n\n### 0.4 The thresholds, with their hypotheses\n\n* **Proposition T** (§6.4, §8.1). *If* for every `c′ > 2 ln 2` there is\n  `I(c′) > 0`, continuous, with `P(no component of G(N, c′/N) exceeds N/2) ≤\n  e^{−(I(c′) − o(1)) N}`, *then* `β_sep(c) > 0` for every `c > 2 ln 2`. The\n  hypothesis is the upper-bound half of the LDP for the largest component on\n  the closed set `[0, ½]`: O'Connell 1998 (not held) as restated by\n  Puhalskii 2005 (Cor. 2.4(3), held) and Andreis–König–Patterson 2021\n  (Cor. 1.3, held); `I_{c′}(½) > 0` iff `c′ > 2 ln 2` on the quoted formula.\n  **Cited, not verified by us as a theorem.** What is verified: the value of\n  the quoted formula against the exact finite computation at seven `c′`\n  (`0.0003–0.002`, §5.3), and the finite rate bounded away from zero at\n  `c = 2, 2.5` to `N = 400`, undecided at `c = 1.5`. The method's threshold\n  was `4 ln 2 = 2.77`; this moves it to `2 ln 2 = 1.39`, the bisection\n  threshold of Luczak–McDiarmid for the same reason; the truth is `1`\n  (Lee–Lee–Oum 2012).\n* **Proposition T-cover** (§7.4). *If* the largest component of the MOSP\n  graph of a random cover has an exponentially small lower tail below its\n  typical fraction `θ(d, μ)`, *then* the separator count's floor is positive\n  wherever `θ > ½`. **The hypothesis is stated in no held paper** (Behrisch\n  2007 and Lagerås–Lindholm 2008 give the law of large numbers only). The\n  half-giant line `θ = ½` sits at excess `e = 0.595, 0.603, 0.658, 0.736,\n  0.816` for `μ = ⅛, ¼, ½, 1, 2`, between loop0010's `e_g(r)` and the pair\n  count's `e = 1`; the ensembles on record cannot confirm it (repaired and\n  connectivity-conditioned generators).\n\n### 0.5 The clumping, decomposed (items 03, 04, 09)\n\nOn instances with exact pathwidth at `n ≤ 24` and `k = pw`, a typical\ninstance has 8–62 exact-size empty pairs; one separator carries one pair and\nits reverse (`X₁/X₂ = 1.03–1.6` with `N` odd), the closure merges `1.3–1.6`\n(graphs) and `1.7–3.3` (covers), the single-swap classes `1.4–2.5`, and **no\nratio grows with `n`** (`0.000 ± 0.003` nats per vertex at `c = 10` against\nthe `0.066` a `0.02` gain needs). The second moment's `e^{0.23–0.39 n}` is a\nstatement about the rare-instance regime at `β*`, where the maximising\noverlap is the pair itself or its reverse perturbed through `S`, not the\nsymmetric table typical instances show. Planting a pair and enumerating the\nothers (`n ≤ 32`, 200 per cell) measures that regime directly: the cluster is\n**two lobes with an empty middle** (perturbations of `P₀` and of its reverse;\nthe moved separator vertices have half the planted-side degree of a typical\none and evict at most one neighbour in 60–87% of cases), the median cluster\ngrows at about half the mean's rate on `G(n, c/n)` (`0.24 ± 0.03` against\n`0.31 ± 0.03` nats per vertex at `c = 6`) and **not at all on `(6, 1)`\ncovers** (median `X′ = 1`, the reversed pair, at every size): loop0010's\n`e^{0.23 n}` is a rare-instance artefact of `E[X²]` there. The union bound's\nwhole slack, `−log E[1/X | P₀ empty]`, is `0.065, 0.039, 0.043` nats per\nvertex at the largest sizes (`0.019, 0.012, 0.015` in `β`), sub-linear in `n`\nover the range; the recombinations through the separator (Lemma Rc, `Z_4`)\nrecover 54%, 79% and 98% of it, the computable `Ẑ₀` a third, and the lower\ntail of every `Z` with a closed-form transform is the event *the planted pair\nis closed*, which is why `β_W = β_closed − 0.0002`.\n\n### 0.6 In stacks, on certified instances (item 11)\n\n600 certified `(6, 1)` covers at `n = m = 30–75` and 543 proved `G(n, 10/n)`\ngraphs at `n = 30–60`, floors at `< 0.01` on the `pw` scale, **zero floors\nabove a certified pathwidth for any count**. At `n = 75` on covers the old\npair's floor is 7.0 stacks below the pathwidth; exact sizes buy 0.8, the\nclosed count 0.8 more, the flips nothing: **1.6 of the seven**. At\n`G(60, 10/60)` the old floor is 5.8 below the mean pathwidth and the\nseparator and closed counts buy **one stack**, the same one. Of the 4.8–5.4\nstacks left, Harper's vertex-isoperimetric bound sits at or above the best\ncount on 1,142 of 1,143 instances and within a stack of the pathwidth\nwherever its branch and bound reaches the forced prefix (`n ≤ 40` on covers,\n`n ≤ 50` on graphs), so **at least 77–93% of the leftover is the union bound\nby that instrument** and at most a stack the necessary condition; at larger\n`n` the level cap binds and the split is the cap's (§11.5). This does not\nagree in size with §0.5's planted `0.012–0.019` in `β` (about one stack at\n`n = 75`): the two instruments see different sizes (`n ≤ 32` against 30–75)\nand different quantities (a planted mean against a deterministic bound at\n`θ = 0.01`), and the reconciliation is open (§0.9).\n\n### 0.7 Kill verdicts\n\n| item | criterion | verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| 01 literature | stop rule: a prior separator first moment with an exact inner probability for pathwidth of `G(n, c/n)` | **did not fire** |\n| 02 lemmas | a counterexample to L1, L1′, L2, L3 | **not met** (310,266 graphs, 4,027,298 closures, zero) |\n| 03 clumping | (1) `X₁/X₂`, `X₁/X₃` grow at `< 0.035` nats per vertex at `c = 10`; (2) `X₁/X₄` grows at `≥ 0.15` | (1) **met** (`0.000 ± 0.003`, `−0.003 ± 0.003`); (2) **not met** |\n| 04 planted | the fork: typical / in between / artefact | `G(n, c/n)`: in between (ratios 0.57, 0.36); covers: **artefact** (0) |\n| 05 inner | separator floor at most one stack over the pair floor at every pilot cell | **met for `c ≥ 6`** (all six cells); 2–3 stacks at `c = 3–4` |\n| 06 constants | `β_sep − β* < 0.02` at `c = 6, 10` | **met** (`+0.0113`, `+0.0038`); separate: `+0.029` at `c = 3`, threshold `2 ln 2` conditional |\n| 07 covers | `β_closed − β* < 0.02` at `(6, 1)`, `(4, 1)` | **met** (`+0.0111`, `+0.0110`); `(8, ½)` at `+0.0211` outside the named cells; zero floor violations on 200 |\n| 08 theorems | a counterexample at `n ≤ 7` | **not met** (zero violations in exact rationals) |\n| 09 weighted | a computable `Z` beating the closed count by `0.02` | **met** (`β_W − β_closed = −0.0002`) |\n| 10 Lean | none | everything of (a)–(d) proved; obstacles named |\n| 11 ledger | none; stop condition: a floor above a certified pathwidth | **did not fire** (1,143 instances) |\n| 12 write-up | none | — |\n\n### 0.8 What this is not\n\n* **Not a new headline constant.** `β_sep`, `β_closed`, `β_W` are valid lower\n  bounds on `lim inf pw/n` under the stated bases; none moves `β*` by `0.02`\n  at `c = 6, 10` or at `(4, 1), (6, 1)`; the gaps \"closed\" are fractions of\n  fitted slopes.\n* **Not a theorem about rates.** Theorem S and Theorem Cl are finite\n  inequalities; every rate is either cited (the LDP, not proved here) or\n  fitted (labelled). `E_bip = E_relax` in rate is exact to `N = 120` and\n  conjectural beyond. Propositions T and T-cover are conditional.\n* **Not asymptotic where it is measured.** The planted cluster is at\n  `n ≤ 32`, the ledger at 30–75, the clumping at `n ≤ 24`; the per-vertex\n  slacks are sub-linear over their ranges and are upper estimates of a rate.\n* **Not a priority claim.** The separator object is in Do–Erde–Kang 2024;\n  the inner rate is O'Connell's; the threshold `2 ln 2` is Luczak–McDiarmid's\n  bisection threshold; \"we found no prior statement\" is the wording.\n* **Not canonical.** The closure is a representative (the `A`-first and\n  `R`-first fixpoints differ on 3–14% of pairs); a union bound needs only a\n  map.\n* **Not re-solved.** No certified value was recomputed; `solutions/` was\n  not read; the only new exact solves are 4,800 fresh graphs at `n ≤ 24`\n  (item 03), layouts kept.\n\n### 0.9 Open\n\n1. **Theorem Cl into Lean**: the product-over-blocks lemma for weighted sums\n   over edge subsets (a session; §10.3). Lemmas P, G, F and Corollary S′ need\n   components of `G − S` as finsets; Lemma J and Theorem Cl-cover need\n   inclusion–exclusion over pattern sets.\n2. **The hypotheses.** (H_G): verify the quoted LDP statement against the\n   held sources in full (O'Connell 1998 is not held). (H_C): an exponentially\n   small lower tail for the giant of a random intersection graph, in no held\n   paper.\n3. **The two instruments.** The planted slack (`0.012–0.019` in `β` at\n   `n ≤ 32`) against the Harper ledger (three quarters of 4–5 stacks at\n   30–75): a Harper run with no level cap at `n = 60–75`, and the planted\n   measurement at `n = 48–64`, would say whether the union bound's slack\n   grows with `n` or the necessary condition's rounding is what the ledger\n   sees.\n4. **A count that merges both lobes.** `Z_4`'s transform (the two-sided and\n   reversed-lobe moves, which need the edge-free pairs inside `G[S]`) has no\n   closed form here and is worth twice `Ẑ₀` at `n = 32`; and a combined\n   count with the closedness condition inside the component law (not a\n   `2^κ` tilt).\n5. **Near the threshold.** `β_sep` at `c = 2–4` is the best lower bound on\n   record and the sandwich to E&M is `5–14×` wide; nothing exact is known\n   there, and the pilot has no fitted slope between `c = 2` and `3`.\n6. **The sparse cover cells.** The closed count passes `0.02` at `(8, ½)` and\n   the additive closed-plus-flip estimate passes it at `μ ≤ 1`, `d = 3–4`; no\n   single count realises both mechanisms.\n7. **The half-giant line on the i.i.d. model**, measured (the ensembles on\n   record are repaired or connectivity-conditioned).\n\n### 0.10 Where everything is\n\nSections 1–11 are the items in order, each with its question, its events,\nits size range, its regenerate command, its kill verdict and what it does not\nclaim. Code: `learning/separator_moment.py` (tested by\n`tests/test_separator_moment.py`, 91 tests); scratch, logs and CSVs under\n`reports/scratch/separator_moment/NN_*/`; Lean in\n`lean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean`; five papers added to\n`literature/` and five recorded missing in `literature/MISSING.md`; the paper's\nAppendix E (`paper1/latex/sec9e_appendix_random.tex`, the paragraph \"Why the\nfirst moment is loose\", the section's closing, five Appendix A rows and seven\nreferences with checked DOIs). Compute: about 8.5 core-hours in all against\n12 planned, 4.9 of them item 11's Harper pass. The paragraph the owner will\nneed for `CLAUDE.md` is the last section of this document.\n\n---\n\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"reports/separator_moment.md\")\ns = p.read_text()\nold_hdr = \"verdict and what it does not claim. §0 (the summary) is written by item\\n12.*\"\nassert s.count(old_hdr) == 1\ns = s.replace(old_hdr, \"verdict and what it does not claim. §0 is the summary (item 12); the\\nparagraph for `CLAUDE.md` is the last section.*\")\nanchor = \"\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Literature: who counts separators\"\nassert s.count(anchor) == 1\nsec0 = Path(\"/tmp/sec0.md\").read_text()\ns = s.replace(anchor, \"\\n---\\n\\n\" + sec0 + \"## 1. Literature: who counts separators\")\np.write_text(s)\nprint(\"inserted\", len(s.splitlines()))\nPYEOF\ngrep -n '^## ' reports/separator_moment.md | head -5","description":"Insert the summary section §0 into the report and update its header"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01STENxjucaL31Sd5cS78U7N":{"cwd":"/home/al/dev/MOSP"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01STENxjucaL31Sd5cS78U7N","type":"tool_result","content":"inserted 4277\n12:## The three events, and the notation\n52:## 0. Summary: what counting events bought, and what it did not (item 12, 2026-11-01)\n343:## 1. Literature: who counts separators, and what the inner probability is known to be (item 01, 2026-11-01)\n655:## 2. The deterministic lemmas: balanced separator, its relaxation, the closed pair (item 02, 2026-11-01)\n963:## 3. The clumping decomposed: pairs, separators, closed pairs and move-classes on instances with exact pathwidth (item 03, 2026-11-01)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"705e2dc1-3bd5-4ca7-a2e8-b0a1809ff2f3","uuid":"8c7040a6-6ad0-4cc0-914e-63df08a6d2ef","timestamp":"2026-11-01T23:06:58.144Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"inserted 4277\n12:## The three events, and the notation\n52:## 0. Summary: what counting events bought, and what it did not (item 12, 2026-11-01)\n343:## 1. Literature: who counts separators, and what the inner probability is known to be (item 01, 2026-11-01)\n655:## 2. The deterministic lemmas: balanced separator, its relaxation, the closed pair (item 02, 2026-11-01)\n963:## 3. The clumping decomposed: pairs, separators, closed pairs and move-classes on instances with exact pathwidth (item 03, 2026-11-01)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/separator_moment.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":6,"oldLines":8,"newStart":6,"newLines":8,"lines":[" moves when the count runs over the **event** a narrow layout forces"," instead of over the **witnesses** of that event. Sections are the items,"," in order; each states its size range, its regenerate command, its kill","-verdict and what it does not claim. §0 (the summary) is written by item","-12.*","+verdict and what it does not claim. §0 is the summary (item 12); the","+paragraph for `CLAUDE.md` is the last section.*"," "," ## The three events, and the notation"," "]},{"oldStart":49,"oldLines":6,"newStart":49,"newLines":297,"lines":[" "," ---"," ","+## 0. Summary: what counting events bought, and what it did not (item 12, 2026-11-01)","+","+**The question.** The first-moment lower bound on the pathwidth of `G(n, c/n)`","+and on the optimum of random MOSP instances (`β*(c)`, `β*(d, μ)`;","+`FirstMoment.lean`, `CliqueCoverMoment.lean`) counts *witnesses* — ordered","+empty pairs `(A, R)` at the forced sizes — and misses the fitted slopes by","+`0.08–0.10` in `β` on `G(n, c/n)` and `0.04–0.06` on covers. loop0010 located","+the slack in the union bound over clustered witnesses. This loop asked whether","+counting the **event** a narrow layout forces — once per separator, once per","+closed pair, or with a weight that divides each witness by the size of its","+cluster — moves the constant, and by how much, and where.","+","+**The answer in one paragraph.** Three new first moments are valid and two","+are theorems in finite form (one in Lean). None moves the headline constants","+by the `0.02` the brief set as worth a page: on `G(n, c/n)` the separator","+count gains `+0.011` at `c = 6` and `+0.004` at `c = 10`, the closed-pair count","+`+0.010` and `+0.008`; on random covers the closed-pair count gains `+0.011`","+at `(d, μ) = (4, 1)` and `(6, 1)`. **The route is closed for the headline","+constants**, as the plan's pre-registered estimates said it would be. What it","+bought instead: a near-threshold gain (`+0.029` at `c = 3`, a third of the gap","+to the fitted slope), the method's threshold moved from `4 ln 2` to `2 ln 2`","+conditional on a cited large-deviation principle, a provable sandwich with the","+published upper line of Edwards & McDermid (2015), a direct measurement of","+what the cluster of witnesses is (two lobes through the separator; on covers","+the reversed pair and nothing else, so loop0010's `e^{0.23 n}` is a","+rare-instance artefact there), the whole union-bound slack as a bounded","+planted statistic (`0.012–0.019` in `β` at `n ≤ 32`), and a ledger in stacks","+on 1,143 certified instances. The literature search found the separator as the","+object of a width first moment once (Do, Erde & Kang 2024, with a","+deterministic inner bound) and the inner rate in a different literature","+(O'Connell 1998); we found no prior statement of the inner probability of the","+bipartition event, nor of its use for a width constant.","+","+### 0.1 The three events, and the weighted identity","+","+With `k < n`, `N = n − k`, `t = ⌈N/2⌉`, `r = N − t`, a layout of vertex","+separation `≤ k` gives at the prefix of size `t` three disjoint sets","+`A ∪ R ∪ S = V`, `|A| = t`, `|R| = r`, `|S| = k`, with no `A–R` edge (L1, §2.1;","+Lean `exists_balanced_separator`). Three events, three counts:","+","+| count | what is counted | one event per |","+|---|---|---|","+| **pair** (on record) | `X` = ordered exact-size empty pairs `(A, R)` | witness |","+| **separator** | `k`-sets `S` with `E_bip(S)`: the components of `G − S` can be grouped into sides of sizes `t`, `r` (`E_relax`: no component larger than `t`; strictly weaker, `3K₂`) | separator |","+| **closed pair** | pairs with `S = N(A) ∩ N(R)`, sides at least the forced sizes, `|S| ≤ k`; the fixpoint of one round of `R* = V ∖ N[A]`, `A* = V ∖ N[R*]` | closed pair |","+| **weighted** | `Y = Σ_P 1[P empty]/Z(P)` for any `1 ≤ Z ≤ X` on the empty pairs; `Y ≥ 1[X > 0]` pointwise, `= 1[X > 0]` at `Z = X` | cluster (as `Z` sees it) |","+","+\"An exact-size pair exists\" and \"some `k`-set is in `E_bip`\" are the same","+event, counted differently (L1′ c). Two identities carry the measurements:","+`E[X′ | P₀ empty] = E[X²]/E[X] − 1` (the second-moment ratio *is* the planted","+mean) and `P(X > 0)/E[X] = E[1/X | P₀ empty]` (the union bound's whole slack is","+a bounded planted statistic).","+","+### 0.2 The ladder, with the status of each rung","+","+| rung | theorem (Lean name) | on paper | measured (size range; section) | fitted | conditional / conjectured |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| L1, L1′ (a, b, d), L2, L3: the structures a narrow layout forces | `exists_balanced_separator`, `exists_balanced_separator_cover`, `exists_isBalancedBip`, `card_componentOff_le_of_isBalancedBip`, `closeStep_isClosedPair`, `closeStep_closeStep`, `exists_closedPair_of_pathwidth_le`, `isClosedPair_iff_sees_both`, … (30 names, §10.1) | L1′ (c) converse, §2.2 | checked on every graph to 9 vertices, 20,000 random at 10–12, 2,000 covers: zero violations (§2.4) | — | — |","+| exact-size pair count | the `Z ≡ 1` instance of `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_weighted` | §8.1 | floors on 200 Chu & Stuckey and 1,143 certified instances (§7.5, §11) | — | — |","+| **Theorem S** (separator count, finite form) | `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_choose_mul_innerBip` (inner probability as a weighted count; relabelling `innerBip_eq_of_card_eq`) | the inner probability by the partition formula (Lemma P) and Gilbert's recursion (Lemmas G, F), §8.1–§8.2; exact to `N = 120` (`E_bip`), `N = 400` (`E_relax`), §5 | `n = 60, 120`, `c = 3–10` in stacks (§5.2, §6.5, §9.6) | the rate of `E_bip` beyond `N = 120`; `β_sep(fitted)` (§6.1) | `β_sep(cited)` rests on the LDP for the largest component (O'Connell 1998 via Puhalskii 2005 Cor. 2.4(3)); `E_bip` and `E_relax` of equal rate beyond `N = 120` (§5.3) |","+| **Theorem Cl** (closed-pair count) | union bound `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_sum_closedPairs`; characterisation `isClosedPair_iff_sees_both` | the independence step and the exact expectation, §8.1; `β_closed` the root of a closed-form exponent, §6.1 (b) | floors (§6.5, §7.5, §11) | — | the supremum at the corner at every `c` (numerical, ten `c`) |","+| Theorem Cl-cover, the NA bound | — | the `(u, w)` inclusion–exclusion, §7.1 (a); the cancellation-free bound by negative association (Joag-Dev & Proschan 1983, cited), §7.1 (a′) | exact against enumeration at `n ≤ 8`; the NA bound's slack a constant `0.2` nats at `n = 8–26` (§7.3) | the NA bound's slope | — |","+| **Lemma W** (weighted count), Lemma Fl (flips), Corollary W-flip | `weightedCount_ge_indicator`, `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_weighted`, `flipPair_*`, `card_flips_le`, `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_flipWeighted` | Lemma J (joint binomial moments), the evaluation of `E[Y]`, §8.1 | `E[Y]` within 1.7 s.e. of 1,000 Monte Carlo covers (§8.3) | — | — |","+| Lemma Rc (recombinations), `Ẑ₀`, `β_W` | — | §9.1, §9.3 (the transform of `Ẑ₀` a binomial sum) | every labelled graph to 6 vertices; planted lower tail at `n ≤ 32` (§9.2) | — | — |","+| the combined count | — | §6.1 (c), valid, not the best | — | fitted only (no LDP for the tilted event) | — |","+| Harper (the necessary condition's instrument) | `exists_closedNbhd_card_le` (`EmptyPair.lean`) | — | 1,143 instances under a level cap and a budget (§11) | — | — |","+| Proposition T (threshold `2 ln 2`), T-cover (half-giant line) | — | §6.4, §7.4, §8.1 | `N ≤ 400` consistent at `c = 2, 2.5`, undecided at `1.5` (§6.4) | — | (H_G) cited, not verified by us; (H_C) stated in no held paper |","+","+Every Lean theorem of the loop is in `lean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean`","+(78 theorems, 21 definitions; no `sorry`, no `axiom`; `propext`,","+`Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound` only, `paper1/axiom_check.lean`); what is on","+paper and not in Lean is named with its obstacle in §10.3 (components of","+`G − S` as finsets; the product-over-blocks lemma; inclusion–exclusion over","+pattern sets).","+","+### 0.3 The constants","+","+`G(n, c/n)` (§6.3, §9.3, §9.6; `constants.csv`, `beta_w.csv`,","+`threshold_fine.csv`). `β_sep` (cited) is the root of","+`H(β) = (1 − β) I(c(1 − β))` with `I` the LDP rate of O'Connell as restated by","+Puhalskii, **cited**; `β_sep` (fitted) uses the log-corrected fit of the exact","+`−log P_N(E_relax)` over `N = 100–400`, **fitted**; `β_closed` and `β_W` are","+roots of closed-form exponents (on paper, the supremum located numerically);","+the slope is the pilot's fitted `β_∞` (survey §7(d), `n ≤ 70–120`,","+**fitted**); E&M is Edwards & McDermid (2015) Cor. 5.2 on Poisson(`c`)","+degrees, the published upper line (owner's note).","+","+| `c` | `β*` | `β_sep` cited | `β_sep` fitted | `β_closed` | `β_W` (`Ẑ₀`) | best valid | fitted slope | E&M upper | share of the gap closed |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| 2 | 0 | 0.0056 | 0.0059 | 0 | 0 | 0.006 | 0.040 | 0.085 | 15% |","+| 2.8 | 0.0008 | 0.0290 | 0.0294 | 0.0008 | 0.0008 | 0.029 | — | 0.162 | — |","+| 3 | 0.0087 | 0.0368 | 0.0374 | 0.0096 | 0.0096 | 0.037 | 0.099 | 0.183 | 32% |","+| 4 | 0.0613 | 0.0827 | 0.0833 | 0.0671 | 0.0671 | 0.083 | 0.158 | 0.285 | 23% |","+| 6 | 0.1706 | 0.1817 | 0.1820 | 0.1803 | 0.1801 | 0.182 | 0.268 | 0.458 | 12% |","+| 8 | 0.2628 | 0.2690 | 0.2691 | 0.2722 | 0.2720 | 0.272 | 0.360 | 0.576 | 10% |","+| 10 | 0.3371 | 0.3409 | 0.3410 | 0.3453 | 0.3451 | 0.345 | 0.415 | 0.656 | 11% |","+| 20 | 0.5535 | 0.5542 | 0.5543 | 0.5573 | 0.5572 | 0.557 | — | 0.826 | — |","+","+The separator count's gain is a sparse-side one and peaks in `β` at the pair","+count's own threshold `c = 4 ln 2` (`+0.029`); the closed count's is a","+dense-side one (the `q` terms, `2β ln q((1 − β)/2)` nats) and wins from","+`c = 8`. The combined count (closed pairs grouped by separator with a `2^κ`","+bound on the colourings) is below the closed count everywhere and below `β*`","+at `c ≤ 4`. Conversion: the pair exponent's slope at `β*` is `5.5, 3.9, 3.4,","+3.3, 3.3` nats per unit of `β` at `c = 3, 4, 6, 8, 10`, so a gain of `g` nats","+per vertex is `g/3.3` in `β` at `c ≥ 6`.","+","+Random clique covers (`m = μ n` patterns of `d` customers, the i.i.d. model of","+`CliqueCoverMoment.lean`; §7.2, `grid.csv`). `β_closed` by the valid","+negative-association bound (the independent-sites approximation differs by","+`≤ 0.001`); `β_flip` the exact weighted count with the flip weight; `b` the","+certified slope of `excess_phase_diagram.md` §2.5 (**measured**, 30–100","+customers); E&M on the cover degree law.","+","+| `(d, μ)` | `β*` | `β_closed` | `β_flip` | best | `b` | E&M upper | share of the gap |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| (4, 1) | 0.2859 | 0.2969 | 0.2917 | 0.297 | 0.348 | 0.660 | 18% |","+| (6, 1) | 0.5132 | 0.5244 | 0.5155 | 0.524 | 0.577 | 0.861 | 18% |","+| (10, 1) | 0.7567 | 0.7614 | 0.7570 | 0.761 | 0.795 | 0.957 | 12% |","+| (8, ½) | 0.3977 | 0.4188 | 0.4039 | 0.419 | 0.463 | 0.831 | 32% |","+| CS 125×125, `d = 2` (pooled sizes) | 0.0983 | 0.1039 | 0.1096 | 0.110 | 0.146 | 0.392 | 24% |","+| CS 125×125, `d = 4` | 0.3208 | 0.3345 | 0.3268 | 0.335 | 0.396 | 0.729 | 18% |","+","+The separator count's constant is not computed on covers (no LDP to cite for","+the giant of a random intersection graph); the closed count is a sparse-side","+gain there, largest at few large patterns (`+0.021` at `(8, ½)`, the one cell","+above `0.02`, outside the kill's named cells); the flips are worth","+`0.001–0.006` at `μ ≥ 1`, `d ≥ 4` and `+0.011` at the Chu & Stuckey `d = 2`","+sizes. E&M is loose on covers (it sees the degrees of a union of cliques, not","+the cliques); the project's own `β⁺` (`excess_phase_diagram.md` §7) is the","+tighter upper end there.","+","+### 0.4 The thresholds, with their hypotheses","+","+* **Proposition T** (§6.4, §8.1). *If* for every `c′ > 2 ln 2` there is","+  `I(c′) > 0`, continuous, with `P(no component of G(N, c′/N) exceeds N/2) ≤","+  e^{−(I(c′) − o(1)) N}`, *then* `β_sep(c) > 0` for every `c > 2 ln 2`. The","+  hypothesis is the upper-bound half of the LDP for the largest component on","+  the closed set `[0, ½]`: O'Connell 1998 (not held) as restated by","+  Puhalskii 2005 (Cor. 2.4(3), held) and Andreis–König–Patterson 2021","+  (Cor. 1.3, held); `I_{c′}(½) > 0` iff `c′ > 2 ln 2` on the quoted formula.","+  **Cited, not verified by us as a theorem.** What is verified: the value of","+  the quoted formula against the exact finite computation at seven `c′`","+  (`0.0003–0.002`, §5.3), and the finite rate bounded away from zero at","+  `c = 2, 2.5` to `N = 400`, undecided at `c = 1.5`. The method's threshold","+  was `4 ln 2 = 2.77`; this moves it to `2 ln 2 = 1.39`, the bisection","+  threshold of Luczak–McDiarmid for the same reason; the truth is `1`","+  (Lee–Lee–Oum 2012).","+* **Proposition T-cover** (§7.4). *If* the largest component of the MOSP","+  graph of a random cover has an exponentially small lower tail below its","+  typical fraction `θ(d, μ)`, *then* the separator count's floor is positive","+  wherever `θ > ½`. **The hypothesis is stated in no held paper** (Behrisch","+  2007 and Lagerås–Lindholm 2008 give the law of large numbers only). The","+  half-giant line `θ = ½` sits at excess `e = 0.595, 0.603, 0.658, 0.736,","+  0.816` for `μ = ⅛, ¼, ½, 1, 2`, between loop0010's `e_g(r)` and the pair","+  count's `e = 1`; the ensembles on record cannot confirm it (repaired and","+  connectivity-conditioned generators).","+","+### 0.5 The clumping, decomposed (items 03, 04, 09)","+","+On instances with exact pathwidth at `n ≤ 24` and `k = pw`, a typical","+instance has 8–62 exact-size empty pairs; one separator carries one pair and","+its reverse (`X₁/X₂ = 1.03–1.6` with `N` odd), the closure merges `1.3–1.6`","+(graphs) and `1.7–3.3` (covers), the single-swap classes `1.4–2.5`, and **no","+ratio grows with `n`** (`0.000 ± 0.003` nats per vertex at `c = 10` against","+the `0.066` a `0.02` gain needs). The second moment's `e^{0.23–0.39 n}` is a","+statement about the rare-instance regime at `β*`, where the maximising","+overlap is the pair itself or its reverse perturbed through `S`, not the","+symmetric table typical instances show. Planting a pair and enumerating the","+others (`n ≤ 32`, 200 per cell) measures that regime directly: the cluster is","+**two lobes with an empty middle** (perturbations of `P₀` and of its reverse;","+the moved separator vertices have half the planted-side degree of a typical","+one and evict at most one neighbour in 60–87% of cases), the median cluster","+grows at about half the mean's rate on `G(n, c/n)` (`0.24 ± 0.03` against","+`0.31 ± 0.03` nats per vertex at `c = 6`) and **not at all on `(6, 1)`","+covers** (median `X′ = 1`, the reversed pair, at every size): loop0010's","+`e^{0.23 n}` is a rare-instance artefact of `E[X²]` there. The union bound's","+whole slack, `−log E[1/X | P₀ empty]`, is `0.065, 0.039, 0.043` nats per","+vertex at the largest sizes (`0.019, 0.012, 0.015` in `β`), sub-linear in `n`","+over the range; the recombinations through the separator (Lemma Rc, `Z_4`)","+recover 54%, 79% and 98% of it, the computable `Ẑ₀` a third, and the lower","+tail of every `Z` with a closed-form transform is the event *the planted pair","+is closed*, which is why `β_W = β_closed − 0.0002`.","+","+### 0.6 In stacks, on certified instances (item 11)","+","+600 certified `(6, 1)` covers at `n = m = 30–75` and 543 proved `G(n, 10/n)`","+graphs at `n = 30–60`, floors at `< 0.01` on the `pw` scale, **zero floors","+above a certified pathwidth for any count**. At `n = 75` on covers the old","+pair's floor is 7.0 stacks below the pathwidth; exact sizes buy 0.8, the","+closed count 0.8 more, the flips nothing: **1.6 of the seven**. At","+`G(60, 10/60)` the old floor is 5.8 below the mean pathwidth and the","+separator and closed counts buy **one stack**, the same one. Of the 4.8–5.4","+stacks left, Harper's vertex-isoperimetric bound sits at or above the best","+count on 1,142 of 1,143 instances and within a stack of the pathwidth","+wherever its branch and bound reaches the forced prefix (`n ≤ 40` on covers,","+`n ≤ 50` on graphs), so **at least 77–93% of the leftover is the union bound","+by that instrument** and at most a stack the necessary condition; at larger","+`n` the level cap binds and the split is the cap's (§11.5). This does not","+agree in size with §0.5's planted `0.012–0.019` in `β` (about one stack at","+`n = 75`): the two instruments see different sizes (`n ≤ 32` against 30–75)","+and different quantities (a planted mean against a deterministic bound at","+`θ = 0.01`), and the reconciliation is open (§0.9).","+","+### 0.7 Kill verdicts","+","+| item | criterion | verdict |","+|---|---|---|","+| 01 literature | stop rule: a prior separator first moment with an exact inner probability for pathwidth of `G(n, c/n)` | **did not fire** |","+| 02 lemmas | a counterexample to L1, L1′, L2, L3 | **not met** (310,266 graphs, 4,027,298 closures, zero) |","+| 03 clumping | (1) `X₁/X₂`, `X₁/X₃` grow at `< 0.035` nats per vertex at `c = 10`; (2) `X₁/X₄` grows at `≥ 0.15` | (1) **met** (`0.000 ± 0.003`, `−0.003 ± 0.003`); (2) **not met** |","+| 04 planted | the fork: typical / in between / artefact | `G(n, c/n)`: in between (ratios 0.57, 0.36); covers: **artefact** (0) |","+| 05 inner | separator floor at most one stack over the pair floor at every pilot cell | **met for `c ≥ 6`** (all six cells); 2–3 stacks at `c = 3–4` |","+| 06 constants | `β_sep − β* < 0.02` at `c = 6, 10` | **met** (`+0.0113`, `+0.0038`); separate: `+0.029` at `c = 3`, threshold `2 ln 2` conditional |","+| 07 covers | `β_closed − β* < 0.02` at `(6, 1)`, `(4, 1)` | **met** (`+0.0111`, `+0.0110`); `(8, ½)` at `+0.0211` outside the named cells; zero floor violations on 200 |","+| 08 theorems | a counterexample at `n ≤ 7` | **not met** (zero violations in exact rationals) |","+| 09 weighted | a computable `Z` beating the closed count by `0.02` | **met** (`β_W − β_closed = −0.0002`) |","+| 10 Lean | none | everything of (a)–(d) proved; obstacles named |","+| 11 ledger | none; stop condition: a floor above a certified pathwidth | **did not fire** (1,143 instances) |","+| 12 write-up | none | — |","+","+### 0.8 What this is not","+","+* **Not a new headline constant.** `β_sep`, `β_closed`, `β_W` are valid lower","+  bounds on `lim inf pw/n` under the stated bases; none moves `β*` by `0.02`","+  at `c = 6, 10` or at `(4, 1), (6, 1)`; the gaps \"closed\" are fractions of","+  fitted slopes.","+* **Not a theorem about rates.** Theorem S and Theorem Cl are finite","+  inequalities; every rate is either cited (the LDP, not proved here) or","+  fitted (labelled). `E_bip = E_relax` in rate is exact to `N = 120` and","+  conjectural beyond. Propositions T and T-cover are conditional.","+* **Not asymptotic where it is measured.** The planted cluster is at","+  `n ≤ 32`, the ledger at 30–75, the clumping at `n ≤ 24`; the per-vertex","+  slacks are sub-linear over their ranges and are upper estimates of a rate.","+* **Not a priority claim.** The separator object is in Do–Erde–Kang 2024;","+  the inner rate is O'Connell's; the threshold `2 ln 2` is Luczak–McDiarmid's","+  bisection threshold; \"we found no prior statement\" is the wording.","+* **Not canonical.** The closure is a representative (the `A`-first and","+  `R`-first fixpoints differ on 3–14% of pairs); a union bound needs only a","+  map.","+* **Not re-solved.** No certified value was recomputed; `solutions/` was","+  not read; the only new exact solves are 4,800 fresh graphs at `n ≤ 24`","+  (item 03), layouts kept.","+","+### 0.9 Open","+","+1. **Theorem Cl into Lean**: the product-over-blocks lemma for weighted sums","+   over edge subsets (a session; §10.3). Lemmas P, G, F and Corollary S′ need","+   components of `G − S` as finsets; Lemma J and Theorem Cl-cover need","+   inclusion–exclusion over pattern sets.","+2. **The hypotheses.** (H_G): verify the quoted LDP statement against the","+   held sources in full (O'Connell 1998 is not held). (H_C): an exponentially","+   small lower tail for the giant of a random intersection graph, in no held","+   paper.","+3. **The two instruments.** The planted slack (`0.012–0.019` in `β` at","+   `n ≤ 32`) against the Harper ledger (three quarters of 4–5 stacks at","+   30–75): a Harper run with no level cap at `n = 60–75`, and the planted","+   measurement at `n = 48–64`, would say whether the union bound's slack","+   grows with `n` or the necessary condition's rounding is what the ledger","+   sees.","+4. **A count that merges both lobes.** `Z_4`'s transform (the two-sided and","+   reversed-lobe moves, which need the edge-free pairs inside `G[S]`) has no","+   closed form here and is worth twice `Ẑ₀` at `n = 32`; and a combined","+   count with the closedness condition inside the component law (not a","+   `2^κ` tilt).","+5. **Near the threshold.** `β_sep` at `c = 2–4` is the best lower bound on","+   record and the sandwich to E&M is `5–14×` wide; nothing exact is known","+   there, and the pilot has no fitted slope between `c = 2` and `3`.","+6. **The sparse cover cells.** The closed count passes `0.02` at `(8, ½)` and","+   the additive closed-plus-flip estimate passes it at `μ ≤ 1`, `d = 3–4`; no","+   single count realises both mechanisms.","+7. **The half-giant line on the i.i.d. model**, measured (the ensembles on","+   record are repaired or connectivity-conditioned).","+","+### 0.10 Where everything is","+","+Sections 1–11 are the items in order, each with its question, its events,","+its size range, its regenerate command, its kill verdict and what it does not","+claim. Code: `learning/separator_moment.py` (tested by","+`tests/test_separator_moment.py`, 91 tests); scratch, logs and CSVs under","+`reports/scratch/separator_moment/NN_*/`; Lean in","+`lean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean`; five papers added to","+`literature/` and five recorded missing in `literature/MISSING.md`; the paper's","+Appendix E (`paper1/latex/sec9e_appendix_random.tex`, the paragraph \"Why the","+first moment is loose\", the section's closing, five Appendix A rows and seven","+references with checked DOIs). Compute: about 8.5 core-hours in all against","+12 planned, 4.9 of them item 11's Harper pass. The paragraph the owner will","+need for `CLAUDE.md` is the last section of this document.","+","+---","+"," ## 1. Literature: who counts separators, and what the inner probability is known to be (item 01, 2026-11-01)"," "," **Question (G of the brief).** Has anyone counted balanced *vertex*"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/separator_moment.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01STENxjucaL31Sd5cS78U7N","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
